    <ResourcePreloader />
    <base href="/" />
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    @* No theme-color meta tag: this site paints one fixed light theme (see bit-theme="light" above),
       so there is nothing for a tag to follow - manifest.json's theme_color carries the same color
       for the installed PWA. A theme switcher here would need the tag back, kept in step with the
       page the way Bit.BlazorUI.Demo.Client.Core/Scripts/app.ts does it. *@
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="description" content="bit is a digital innovation company with software development at its core. We help out our customers innovate with designing and building their digital products efficiently with our Agile mindset and lean processes." />
    <Link rel="icon" Href="/favicon.ico" type="image/x-icon" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode=RenderModeProvider.Current />
    <Link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="512x512" Href="images/icons/bit-icon-512.png" />
    @* iOS ignores the manifest when it launches an installed app and shows a blank white screen until the first paint, unless one of
       these launch images matches the device's screen exactly. One per iPhone / iPad screen and orientation, drawn from the
       manifest's background_color and the app icon; plain links rather than <Link>, as none of them is ever fetched by a browser
       other than iOS, and only once, when the app is added to the home screen. *@
